  "description_short": "Family-run country cafe in Hoekwil serving homemade bakes, hearty breakfasts, and fresh farm fare.",
  "description_long": "Tucked away in the quiet village of Hoekwil between Wilderness and George, this charming country cafe feels like stepping into a friend's farmhouse kitchen. The smell of fresh bread and cakes baking draws you in, while the relaxed atmosphere and playground keep families settled for hours.\n\nThe menu focuses on honest country cooking — think generous breakfast platters, homemade pies, farm-fresh eggs, and cakes that disappear fast. Everything's made on-site, from the bread to the preserves lining the shelves. It's the kind of place where locals pop in for their weekly bread and visitors discover by happy accident.\n\nSet at the crossroads of DuiweRivier Road and Church Street, it's an easy detour off the N2 when you need a proper coffee and something sweet. The adjoining farm store stocks local produce and homemade goods, making it a handy stop for self-caterers exploring the Garden Route.",
